disease-syndicate-foodborne-name = engineered enterovirus
disease-syndicate-foodborne-description = An engineered foodborne strain causing gastrointestinal symptoms. Transmitted only by consuming contaminated food or drinks.
disease-hint-syndicate-foodborne = Repeated artificial insertions detected in the genome: the strain is adapted for foodborne infection and does not spread by touch or droplets. Deliberate culture contamination is likely; inspect the patient's food and drinks.
